spout should end above basin but still behind rim. From viewer, tip can be visible above rim at y=784. Current tip at 776, fine. Maybe just lengthen to 783.\n\nNeed fix cabinet flatness maybe add slight reflections. Color grade helped. Could add a warm sun stripe on cabinets? It would be subtle. Perhaps add two angled translucent light patches on cabinet fronts near x=800..1150 y=905..1100. But the scene's lower area would feel more atmospheric. Add:\n```\nlight = layer polygon [(700,900),(1020,900),(1150,1200),(830,1200)] alpha 16 warm; blur 30\n```\nNo need.\n\nCould add a cat's tail? done.\n\nWhat about the top left curtain rod has ball finials; okay.\nTop right wall empty but shelf fills.\n\nMaybe add a tiny wall clock above shelves? No space: shelf at y=288, ceiling 0. Could put at x=1050,y=130, but plates at y=170. Empty top center wall x850..1000 could use a small brass wall hook? not necessary.\n\nWe should ensure final looks \"cozy kitchen in the morning\", which it does. User likely not expecting photorealism, and this is charming. Could deliver.\n\nBut let's iterate one more time to remove ghost steam, soften beams, maybe add a little more warmth to window and reduce the huge sun disk? Let's inspect window crop. Maybe it's fine."}
